# ── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Postgres. SQLite was the engine until the move to Vercel — a serverless
# function has no writable disk, so a file-backed database cannot be read or
# written there. Any Postgres works; Neon and Supabase both have free tiers.
#
# The same URL is used locally. There is no SQLite fallback any more: running
# two engines means the case-sensitivity of `contains` differs between a
# developer's machine and production, which is exactly the class of bug that
# does not show up until somebody searches in lowercase.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host/database?sslmode=require"

# ── Admin portal ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Both are required. Without ENABLE_ADMIN the /admin routes return 404,
# exactly like any unknown path, so the portal cannot leak into a
# production deploy by accident.
#
#   ENABLE_ADMIN    whether /admin exists at all
#   ADMIN_PASSWORD  the shared credential, checked server-side
#
# ENABLE_ADMIN=true
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=choose-something-long

# Optional. Without a key the map renders on MapLibre + OpenFreeMap.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_MAP_ID=

# ── Real station data ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Free key: https://openchargemap.org/site/develop/api
# With it set, "npm run import:stations" pulls real Pakistani charging
# stations into the database. Without it, stations are added by hand at
# /admin/stations. Nothing is ever generated — see scripts/import-stations.ts.
OPENCHARGEMAP_API_KEY=

# ── Sessions ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Signs the login cookie for business owners. Generate with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('base64url'))"
# Falls back to ADMIN_PASSWORD in development only. Set it for real
# deployments — sharing one secret means one leak compromises both.
SESSION_SECRET=

# ─── Admin portal ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Two independent gates, because they fail differently — see
# src/lib/admin-auth.ts.
#
#   ENABLE_ADMIN    whether /admin exists at all. Enforced in middleware, so
#                   anything other than exactly "true" makes every /admin URL
#                   return a 404 identical to an unknown path: no login form,
#                   no hint a portal is there. This is why /admin appeared not
#                   to exist.
#   ADMIN_PASSWORD  the shared password for the sign-in form. One credential
#                   for the whole portal — there are no admin user accounts.
#
# Left off in the template on purpose. A fresh clone should not expose the
# portal by default — set it to true only once ADMIN_PASSWORD is set to
# something real, or /admin is reachable with no password that can open it.
ENABLE_ADMIN=false
ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# ── Automated crawling ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Two independent gates on the HTTP trigger at /api/crawler/daily, for
# the same reason the admin portal has two — see src/lib/crawler-trigger.ts.
#
#   CRAWLER_ENABLED         whether the route exists at all. Anything other
#                           than exactly "true" makes it return 404, identical
#                           to a path that was never built. THIS IS THE
#                           ACTIVATION SWITCH FOR UNATTENDED CRAWLING.
#   CRAWLER_TRIGGER_SECRET  who may fire it. Sent as "Authorization: Bearer
#                           <secret>", never as a query parameter — a secret in
#                           a URL is written to every access log it passes
#                           through. Minimum 32 characters; generate with:
#                             node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64url'))"
#
# Left off in the template deliberately. The command-line path
# (`npm run crawl:daily`) needs neither of these and is the recommended way
# to run a scheduled crawl where a shell is available; the route exists for
# hosts where one is not. Read docs/PHASE4-PRODUCTION-CHECK.md before
# setting CRAWLER_ENABLED.
CRAWLER_ENABLED=false
CRAWLER_TRIGGER_SECRET=

# ── Image uploads ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set automatically by Vercel when a Blob store is attached to the project.
# Leave it unset locally: without it, admin uploads write to public/uploads
# exactly as they always did, so the portal works on a developer machine with
# no cloud account. See src/lib/db/upload-actions.ts.
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=""
